{
  "title": "Image URLs are stored with HTML entities instead of decoded \
characters",
  "description": "`image_urls` entries preserve HTML entity encodings from the \
source's meta tags instead of decoding them, producing URLs that look escaped \
and may not work for downstream consumers that don't re-decode.\n\
\n\
Example from \
data/pipeline-snapshots/smittenkitchen-com_2009-09-grilled-lamb-kebabs-tzatziki.json: \
the image URL is \
'https://i0.wp.com/smittenkitchen.com/wp-content/uploads//2015/05/grilled-lamb-kebabs-tzatziki1.jpg?fit=500%2C333&#038;ssl=1'. \
The `&#038;` comes straight from the `<meta property=\"og:image\">` attribute \
and should be decoded to `&` before it hits the snapshot.\n\
\n\
Fix: HTML-entity-decode URLs extracted from attribute values before storing \
them.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 4,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "pipeline",
    "extraction",
  ],
  "created_at": "2026-04-20T09:33:56-07:00",
  "updated_at": "2026-04-20T09:33:56-07:00",
}
